<poml>
  <meta>
    <id>meta.plan.poml-go-sdk</id>
    <version>0.2.0</version>
    <owner>poml-go-sdk</owner>
  </meta>
  <role>Prioritize Extended POML parity, then Python SDK parity; everything else waits.</role>

  <task caption="Priority 1: Extended POML parity">
    <list>
      <item>See <cp>extended_parity.plan.poml</cp> for the full end-to-end breakdown (schema/enums → converters → goldens → docs).</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Priority 2: Python SDK parity">
    <list>
      <item>See <cp>python_parity.plan.poml</cp> for the end-to-end breakdown.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Priority 3: Tracing parity">
    <list>
      <item>See <cp>tracing_parity.plan.poml</cp> for trace spans/seeds/fixtures toward Python parity.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Backlog (after parity)">
    <list>
      <item>Benchmark parity vs other SDKs (benchmarks.plan.poml).</item>
      <item>Badge/test expansion (fuzz, matrix, lint/vuln) — maintenance only.</item>
      <item>MCP/CLI feature extensions (search/auth/patch/diff) — defer until parity is done.</item>
      <item>Quality governance: keep gofmt + go test ./... required; refer to go.quality.poml.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <log>
    <entry date="2025-11-28" actor="ai.assistant">Rewritten to focus on Extended parity and Python parity; moved other items to backlog.</entry>
  </log>

  <output-format>Keep concise; update after each priority lands.</output-format>
</poml>
